# Integrations and config

Express service under `src/` only.

## RabbitMQ

Code lives in `src/rabbit-mq/`. The connection is `config/rabbit-mq.js`.

Reuse one channel. Manual ack (`noAck: false`). Durable queues. Validate the payload before processing. On success `ack`. On failure `nack(msg, false, false)`. RPC replies include `correlationId` and `replyTo`.

```javascript
channel.consume(queue, async (msg) => {
  try {
    const data = JSON.parse(msg.content.toString());
    // process…
    channel.ack(msg);
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error('Error processing message:', JSON.stringify(error));
    channel.nack(msg, false, false);
  }
}, { noAck: false });
```

Do not auto-ack, and do not ack outside try/catch.

Declare the queue with a dead-letter exchange. Keep `nack(msg, false, false)` so a failed message is not requeued in a loop. The dead-letter queue holds it. Do not nack into a queue that has no dead-letter destination.

## Cron

Jobs live in `src/crons/` and register through `src/crons/index.js`, which `index.js` requires. Every scheduled callback has try/catch and logs the failure.

```javascript
cron.schedule('* * * * *', async () => {
  try {
    await updateNonCancelledOrders();
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error('Cron job failed:', error);
  }
});
```

## Socket.IO

Initialized in `app.js` as `global.io`, path `/empService`. Verify the JWT with `verify(token, config.jwt.secret)` before joining. Join a `socketId` room and emit with `io.to(room).emit(...)`. Persist the connection on the `Socket` model and update it on disconnect.

```javascript
io.to(`${storeId}-manager`).emit('orders', storeOrders);
```

Do not `io.emit` the full dataset, and do not skip the token check on connection.

## Email and uploads

Send mail through `email.service.js` and `mail-templates/`. The transport is `config.email.smtp`. Verify the connection outside tests. Do not hardcode HTML in a controller.

Uploads go through `parser.service.js`: formidable, a size limit, and a streaming upload to S3. ACL is private. Serve a short-lived presigned URL. Check type and size on the server.

## Config

Every secret comes from the environment and is validated with Joi in `config/config.js`. Read `config.jwt.secret` and `config.mongoose.url`. Never inline a secret. `.env` stays gitignored. When `NODE_ENV === 'test'`, the database URL gets a `-test` suffix.
